# Build output. 1.7 GB here, and every byte of it is reproducible from source.
/target/

# Layout backups taken by hand before a redesign. Useful locally, meaningless
# to anyone else, and they go stale the moment `web/` moves on.
web-backup-*/

# Screenshots written into the working directory by the browser tests. They are
# evidence for one run, not artefacts of the project.
#
# The names come from the tests themselves: `fork.png`, `menu-baru.png`,
# `setting.png`, `shellpick.png`, `agent-<theme>.png`, `warna-<theme>.png` —
# plus whatever a one-off debugging script happens to write. Ignoring `*.png`
# at the repository root covers all of them, and `web/` keeps its own assets
# because this rule is anchored to the root.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.gif

# Left behind by the Python helper scripts used for large mechanical edits.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Never commit a daemon home. It holds `config.toml`, and `config.toml` holds
# the token — anyone with that token gets a shell on the machine. The real one
# lives in `~/.sessionhub/`, outside this tree, but a copy dragged in here for
# testing must not follow it to a remote.
.sessionhub/
**/fakehome/
**/farhome/

# Same reasoning, for anything holding credentials in the open. `.env-ssh` —
# the SSH details for the Mac — lives outside this tree today, and this line is
# what keeps a stray copy from following the project to a remote.
.env
.env.*
.env-*
*.pem
id_rsa*

# Logs.
*.log

# A personal notification sound, if one was dropped in (web/notify.mp3|wav|ogg
# — chime.js picks it up by name). It is the user's own file, often ripped from
# somewhere with its own licence, and must not travel with the repo.
/web/notify.mp3
/web/notify.wav
/web/notify.ogg

# SSH credentials for the test Mac live one folder above this repo; this line
# is the fence in case a copy ever strays inside.
.ssh-mac

# Screenshots some tests drop next to themselves rather than at the root.
tests/manual/*.png
